<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bay of Bengal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bay of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> is the north-eastern arm of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>, bordered by eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, Bangladesh, Myanmar and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> at its south-western edge. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmaputra">Brahmaputra</a> and Irrawaddy flow into it. Since ancient times its sea routes linked the ports of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinga">Kalinga</a>, Bengal, Arakan and lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bay-of-bengal.jpg" alt="Bay of Bengal" width="320" height="326" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. NormanEinstein assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bay_of_Bengal_map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
